# Separation of powers (ported from RoseLohr/roses-food-blog CODEOWNERS; same
# role): the gate, the review panel, and the frozen-methodology governance
# surfaces must NOT be modifiable by the same identity that writes the code
# they gate, without a separate explicit approval by the responsible role. In
# this solo setup without a separate policy repo, this is the structural
# substitute: changes to any protected path below require the owner's own
# distinct sign-off.
#
# ENFORCEMENT STATUS (kept accurate on purpose — a stale note here is a claim
# the repository makes about itself, and those are what the claims ledger
# exists to catch):
#   Required status checks   ACTIVE. A ruleset on main requires "test (3.12)"
#                            and "image", with no bypass actors. A direct push
#                            to main is rejected.
#   Code Owner review        NOT enabled, and deliberately so. GitHub does not
#                            accept a self-approval, so requiring it in a
#                            single-maintainer repository would deadlock every
#                            pull request — and a gate that can never pass is a
#                            gate someone removes under pressure. Recorded as
#                            an accepted residual in
#                            audit/06-residual-risk-register.md, with the
#                            compensating control named there.
# So the list below is, today, a machine-checked INVENTORY of the surfaces that
# must not move without the owner (scripts/regime/separation_check.py fails CI
# when one is uncovered) rather than a merge-blocking approval rule.

# The deterministic gate and the review panel itself
/.github/               @mglaeser
/scripts/               @mglaeser

# The audit ledger and the constitution: the evidence a reader would use to
# check any of the above. B-35 extends the gate/gated separation to these.
/governance/            @mglaeser
/audit/                 @mglaeser

# The alert system's decision surfaces: the rules and phrases are the thing
# that decides whether a human gets woken up.
/app/alerts/                        @mglaeser
/config/alert_rules.v3.2.yaml       @mglaeser
/config/alert_phrases.v3.2.json     @mglaeser
/config/alert_phrases.v3.3.json     @mglaeser
/config/alert_phrases.v3.4.json     @mglaeser

# The frozen-methodology governance surfaces (F-01/L-07)
/frozen_methodology.json            @mglaeser
/app/methodology.py                 @mglaeser
/tests/test_frozen_methodology.py   @mglaeser
/docs/GOVERNANCE_FREEZE_RULE.md     @mglaeser
/docs/PINS_DECISION_MEMO.md         @mglaeser
/docs/PIN_EVIDENCE_PACK.md          @mglaeser
/docs/PIN_EVIDENCE_PACK_2.md        @mglaeser
